# pdftk — real-world examples

## Concatenate PDFs into one

```sh
pdftk *.pdf cat output all.pdf
pdftk 1.pdf 2.pdf 3.pdf cat output 123.pdf
```

## Mix pages from multiple files

```sh
# Pages 1-5 of first.pdf followed by page 3 of second.pdf
pdftk A=first.pdf B=second.pdf cat A1-5 B3 output new.pdf
```

## Extract a page range

```sh
pdftk manual.pdf cat 2-4 output excerpt.pdf
```

## Split a PDF into single pages

```sh
pdftk big.pdf burst output page_%02d.pdf
```

## Rotate pages

```sh
# Rotate all pages 90 degrees clockwise (east)
pdftk in.pdf cat 1-endeast output rotated.pdf
```

## Remove a password (when you know it)

```sh
pdftk secured.pdf input_pw PROMPT output unsecured.pdf
```

## Homelab: merge scanned receipts into one file

```sh
pdftk ~/scans/receipt-*.pdf cat output ~/Documents/receipts-$(date +%Y-%m).pdf
```

| Operation | What it does                         |
| --------- | ------------------------------------ |
| cat       | concatenate/select/rotate pages      |
| burst     | split into one file per page         |
| input_pw  | supply password for encrypted input  |
